\par\par \b \uc2  Euro hits new high, dollar wins reprieve vs yen. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Hideyuki Sano \par \uc2 904 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 2002\par 07:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 24 (Reuters) - The dollar hit a 26-month low against the euro on Monday morning, remaining under pressure as U.S. stocks continue to be hurt by economic uncertainty, geopolitical concerns and questions about corporate accounting. \par \par \uc2  The greenback won a brief reprieve against the yen thanks to wariness about Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but it quickly ran out of steam as doubts grew over the Japanese government's stance. \par \par \uc2  As of 0222 GMT, the euro was holding firm against the dollar at 97.20/25 cents, after briefly hitting a 26-month high of 97.30. It was at 97.10/15 in late U.S. trade on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was aided by buying from Japanese investors, which helped raise the euro to 117.87/8.01 yen against 117.66/82. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the euro was likely to remain the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of choice for now, given investors' discomfort with the dollar and doubts on U.S. stocks. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the Dow Jones industrial average fell 1.9 percent after a report that a subsidiary of drug firm Merck & Co. may have inflated its revenues. \par \par \uc2  The tech-heavy Nasdaq Composite lost 1.6 percent to threaten its post-September 11 low. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the dollar was quoted at 121.30/36 yen, a touch above Friday's late U.S. level of 121.05/15 yen but off Monday's high of 121.75 \par \par \uc2  The dollar recovered more than a half yen from a seven-month low of 120.80 yen set in overseas trade on Friday, as Tokyo dealers cut their dollar short positions to prepare for possible dollar-buying by Japanese monetary authorities. \par \par \uc2  NO CHANGE IN \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  POLICY? \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on at least four days in the last several weeks when the dollar fell below 124 yen. But it refrained from doing so last Friday when the dollar fell below that level. \par \par \uc2  Doubts have arisen about possible Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said last Friday that the ministry had no power to dominate the market. \par \par \uc2  His comments surprised many dealers, who had expected him to repeat his usual mantra that the ministry would act in the market if rates moved too quickly. \par \par \uc2  "Shiokawa's comments changed the whole atmosphere," said Fumihiko Kawano, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Nomura Securities. \par \par \uc2  "We can only guess his intentions. But the most plausible explantion seems to be that there was some sort of accord to rectify a strong dollar in the G7 meeting last week," he said, echoing views shared by many in the market. \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa said on Monday he has asked his staff to examine developments in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, though it was not immediately clear what his comment signified. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, senior Finance Ministry official Mizoguchi Zembei said recent movements in the dollar/yen rate were excessive and that the ministry is closely watching the market. \par \par \uc2  But his comments hardly wiped out market suspicions about a possible shift in Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar could fall further versus the yen as the market may want to test how much Japan conceded at the G7. Did it agree to accept the dollar's fall to 120 yen or 115 yen?" said Kawano of Nomura Securities. \par \par \uc2  On the other hand, the yen had its own woes as the stock market benchmark Nikkei average fell to a fresh four-month low, threatening to break below the key 10,000 threshold. \par \par \uc2  With the Nikkei below that level, many Japanese banks would have problems at their book-closings because their stock holdings would carry losses, limiting room to write off their huge bad loans. \par \par \uc2  "There won't be fresh yen-buying to buy Japanese assets any more," said Koji Fukaya, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi. \par \par \uc2  "It's hard to imagine some one will buy the yen for the dollar aggressively. I think the dollar is unlikely to fall much beyond 120 even if \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market," " he added. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the dollar also hit a 2 = year low against the Swiss franc at 1.5085 francs on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was struggling around 1.5097/02 francs \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0258 GMT. All data taken from Reuters with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 GMT. \par \par \uc2   Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   2001 Cls \par \par \uc2   21 Jun. \par \par \uc2   ---------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/dlr       0.9724   0.9705   +0.20    +9.21   0.8904\par  Dlr/yen        121.10   121.09   +0.01    -8.00   131.63\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/yen    117.76   117.54   +0.19    +0.44   117.24\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Dlr/swiss      1.5094   1.5109   -0.10    -9.04   1.6594\par  Stg/dlr        1.4982   1.4970   +0.08    +3.03   1.4541\par  Can/dlr        1.5189   1.5201   -0.08    -4.57   1.5917\par  Aus/dlr        0.5744   0.5741   +0.05   +12.50   0.5106\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/swiss  1.4662   1.4663   -0.01    -0.80   1.4780\par \f28 \