\par\par \b \uc2  Japan Govt Bonds End Lower On Selling Before 10-Yr Tender \b0\par\par\uc2 898 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 2002\par 09:03\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- Japanese government bonds closed slightly lower Monday on profit-taking and hedge-selling before the 10-year bond tender Tuesday, bond traders and analysts said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets via the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  sent the dollar surging against the yen and helped stock markets rise, but had little effect on JGB markets as bond dealers judged that the overall bearish trend toward both the dollar and worldwide stock markets remained unaffected. \par \par \uc2  Around 0600 GMT, the yield on the newest No. 239 10-year JGB closed at 1.315%, down 0.005 from Friday. \par \par \uc2  The lead September 10-year JGB futures closed down 0.03 from Friday at 138.81, but off a session low of 138.75. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  will auction Y1.8 trillion in the July 10-year JGB tender on Tuesday. JGB traders hedged new long-positions prior to the tender, and hedge-selling was cited as one reason September 10-year futures fell. \par \par \uc2  Stronger stocks have recently been viewed as positive for bonds in Japan as banks and other financial institutions which hold large amounts of equities can increase their risk-taking ability and avoid selling bonds to cover stock related losses. \par \par \uc2  But the trend reverted to normal today, with stocks up in the afternoon and JGB futures remaining weak. \par \par \uc2  "The rise in the Nikkei was offset by concerns over high JGB prices," said Soichi Okuda, senior economist at Aozora Bank. \par \par \uc2  The Nikkei 225 Stock Average closed up 116.97 points at 10471.32. \par \par \uc2  "The JGB market was thin. Some investors seemed to have bought cash JGBs but their buying wasn't so active compared to Friday," said Daisuke Uno, chief market analyst at Sumitomo Mitsui Banking Corp. \par \par \uc2  Lead September 10-year JGB futures opened higher following bullish sentiment following on from Friday but the contract couldn't break 138.94 resistance. \par \par \uc2  The yield on the No. 239 10-year and No. 56 20-year bonds fell to year-lows of 1.310% and 1.955% respectively, as investors bought. \par \par \uc2  Japanese authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Monday to curb the yen's surge, Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said. \par \par \uc2  The authorities "took appropriate action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," Shiokawa said in a statement. Some players believed the MOF had abandoned \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a tool to curb the yen's rise for the time being. \par \par \uc2  Prices as of 0600 GMT: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Tiffe Dec 3-Mos Euroyen Price:      99.895  Unchanged\par    SGX Dec 3-Mos Euroyen Price:        99.895  Unchanged\par    TSE Sep  5Y JGB Future Price:        N/A     N/A\par    TSE Sep 10Y JGB Future Price:       138.81  Down 0.03\par    SGX Sep 10Y JGB Future Price:       138.85  Up   0.01\par    10-Yr 1.4% JGB No. 239 Yield:       1.315%  Down 0.005\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The recent drop in the yield on the No.239 10-year cash bonds will\par likely pave the way for the MOF to set the coupon of the July 10-year\par JGB at 1.3%, lower than the 1.4% coupon of the No. 239 bonds.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par If the coupon is set at 1.3%, it will mark the lowest level for a\par 10-year bond coupon since the July 2001 bond, which had a coupon of 1.2%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Investors, such as regional banks, credit associations and life\par insurers, are expected to show healthy demand for the new bonds mainly\par because there are no other instruments in which to invest their cash.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Makoto Yamashita, strategist at UFJ Tsuba Securities, said demand for\par the new bonds from cash-rich investors remains strong. But the upcoming\par release of the BOJ's June tankan corporate sentiment survey due July 1\par and concerns over JGB profit-taking before the end of the first fiscal\par half to September could discourage investors from actively buying.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sumitomo Mitsui's Uno said: "It is questionable whether investors who\par are short on cash JGBs will purchase JGBs at current high levels. They\par don't need to buy new bonds at the tender... they could just buy them in\par the secondary market. But I'm not worried about the result."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Aozora Bank's Okuda said: "The result of the 5-year tender (on July 4)\par after the BOJ's tankan will be more informative as to the state of the\par JGB market than the 10-year bond tender."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par JGB markets remained steady on the back of healthy buying by city\par banks for medium-term JGBs, mainly 5-year, he said. Thus whether city\par banks bid actively or not at the tender remains a key factor for the\par market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The BOJ will hold a one-day policy meeting Wednesday against a\par background of a steadily rising yen and fragile stock markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The strong yen and weak Nikkei remain a source of anxiety for the\par board members. But any concrete adverse impact from those factors on the\par economy or corporate sentiment aren't yet evident in data. So a further\par easing of policy is unlikely," said a senior money trader at a major\par money brokerage firm.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The result of the BOJ's June tankan corporate sentiment survey will be\par closely watched by BOJ officials for evidence of the impact of a strong\par yen and weak stock market on the corporate sector.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   -By Hiroshi Inoue, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-9203;\par hiroshi.inoue@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1037 4153 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020624dy6o000dv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
