\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr/Yen Volatile Amid MOF  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Fears \b0\par\par\uc2  By Audrey McAvoy \par \uc2 643 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 2002\par 07:44\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The dollar and the yen seesawed in volatile Asian trade Friday, as market players fretted over the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets by Japanese authorities. \par \par \uc2  But concern about \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  preventing its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from rising failed to affect the basic negative market sentiment towards the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Investors continue to "lower their exposure" to U.S. assets and shift funds into assets denominated in euro and other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a Japanese brokerage said. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar is very heavy. It's not speculators but investors that are moving their money," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Statements from \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials that they remain ready to step into the market to stem gains posted by the Japanese unit lifted the dollar in early trade, as did speculation the MOF was actually selling yen. \par \par \uc2  "We are watching the markets extremely closely," Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Haruhiko Kuroda told reporters Friday, adding there is no change in the ministry's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance. \par \par \uc2  "As I've been saying, there's absolutely no reason for the yen to strengthen," Kuroda added. \par \par \uc2  Underscoring the sensitivity of the market, a mistaken interpretation that a particular bank was acting on behalf of the ministry and the Bank of Japan when it was buying dollars sent the U.S. unit to a high of Y124.00. \par \par \uc2  But the greenback soon fell back once speculation the authorities had launched a new round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  proved unfounded. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT (1.15 a.m. EDT), the dollar was quoted at Y123.36, below Y123.53 late Thursday in New York. The dollar was at Y124.00 late Thursday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $0.9662, up from $0.9651 late Thursday in New York. The euro was at $0.9582 in Tokyo Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y119.19, down from Y119.22 in New York late Thursday. The euro was at Y118.82 in Tokyo late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.5007, up from $1.4985 in New York and $1.4915 in Tokyo Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was thrown into some confusion however, when Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa made remarks interpreted by some as signaling the ministry would accept a stronger yen. \par \par \uc2  "It's natural for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates to move up and down, and if we fret over such moves we will lose sight of overall economic conditions," Shiokawa told a press conference. \par \par \uc2  "We can't control the markets. All we can do in terms of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy is say we are always alertly watching markets," Shiokawa said. \par \par \uc2  U.S. funds and other players bought the yen on the comments, helping the dollar slide back to around Y123.30. \par \par \uc2  "He seemed to be saying nothing can be done about the stronger yen," a trader at a Japanese bank said. \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa added at the same press conference, however, that if movements are too drastic, the government will look into reasons behind such moves and take those reasons "into consideration," indicating MOF's willingness to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market if necessary. \par \par \uc2  Traders also noted Kuroda and his deputy, Zembei Mizoguchi were consistent with earlier statements, underscoring there has been no shift in the ministry's willingness to step into the market to halt the yen's rise. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   -By Audrey McAvoy, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929;\par audrey.mcavoy@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The chart of late Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates that accompanied Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has\par been replaced with an enhanced \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fixture, which is\par updated hourly.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Subscribers can find this table:\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX\par -0\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020621dy6l0009t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
