\par\par \b \uc2  ANALYSIS-G7 content with dollar weakness, Asia unhappy. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sumeet Desai \par \uc2 816 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juni 2002\par 16:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 19 (Reuters) - Group of Seven finance ministers meeting last weekend appeared happy enough with the dollar's recent decline but in Asia, for instance, not everyone is so pleased the greenback's seven-year bull-run appears at an end. \par \par \uc2  The dollar has fallen 7.5 percent against the euro this year. It has also fallen six percent against the yen and retreated against a host of other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as U.S. assets have started losing their appeal. \par \par \uc2  U.S. policymakers are probably secretly cheering the dollar's fall, although the official line remains that a strong dollar is in U.S. interests. \par \par \uc2  The Europeans aren't even being secretive. But in export-dependent Asia, more countries are becoming worried that the dollar's slide could derail economic recovery. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Taiwan have already \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell their own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the greenback. Korea has said it will also act if exporters' competitiveness is threatened. Australia has stressed the importance of a competitive exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  "The obvious casualty of the dollar's weakness is Japan which can't afford to have a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , its stock market and economy are still too fragile," said Russell Jones, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at Lehman Brothers. \par \par \uc2  "Asian economies are also very sensitive to competitiveness issues and then there is the matter of deflation." \par \par \uc2  April consumer prices fell 0.9 percent in Japan, by 1.1 percent in Singapore, and by 3.1 percent in Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said that further rises in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar would push prices down even more, hurting consumption as purchases were deferred in the hope of getting them cheaper. \par \par \uc2  "The bottom line is deflation, lower interest rates and possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Jones. \par \par \uc2  "You could even see coordinated Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with Korea, Singapore and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  at least." \par \par \uc2  Although coordinated Asian action would be a first, analysts noted there has been a great deal more cooperation between the region's central banks since the 1997 Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis. \par \par \uc2  DOUBLE-EDGED SWORD \par \par \uc2  But lower interest rates than otherwise necessary could also help spur growth and so \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength can also be a good thing, aside from competitiveness concerns. That's why eurozone policymakers have expressed their delight with the euro's rise. \par \par \uc2  "You might get a virtuous circle. The rise in the euro delays interest rate rises which is seen helping recovery and so pushes up the euro further," said Michael Metcalfe, senior strategist at State Street. \par \par \uc2  "That would be a reversal of the vicious circle we saw in September 2000." \par \par \uc2  Back then, the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was forced to raise interest rates and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy euros even as the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued falling to its life lows. \par \par \uc2  The United States, whose exporters have long been complaining that the dollar is overvalued, also stands to benefit from a continued gentle fall in the dollar. \par \par \uc2  That might reduce its huge current account deficit and lower the risk of an even sharper correction later. Even Federal Reserve chairman Alan Greenspan has warned that the deficit will eventually have to be restrained. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said that the U.S.'s strong dollar mantra had become almost meaningless and that the administration would probably welcome the recent decline in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The U.S. might sing the strong dollar song but that applies to a wide spectrum of exchange rates," said Jones. \par \par \uc2  Corporate America also stands to gain from the dollar's weakness as overseas earnings now account for around 20 percent of total U.S. corporate profits. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the world's number one restaurant chain McDonalds said it had raised its earnings forecast because a weak dollar would offset tepid sales. \par \par \uc2  LATIN AMERICA \par \par \uc2  Further dollar weakness would probably prove painful for Latin America although domestic problems in the region mean that countries like Brazil are \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar rather than weaken it. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said that longer term, more falls in the dollar would hurt Latin countries as commodities are priced in dollars and they would also lose competitiveness in U.S. markets. \par \par \uc2  The euro's rise against the dollar also makes it easier for the British government to press for membership of the euro if it were to call a referendum on the issue as the euro's weakness versus the pound has been cited as an obstacle to entry. \par \par \uc2  Dollar weakness against the euro has pushed sterling to a 2-1/2 year low versus the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this month. \par \par \uc2  Eastern European countries, which have long complained about the weakness of the euro, may also benefit if the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rallies further against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "In the end, so much depends on whether dollar weakness is accompanied with U.S. recovery or whether we see dollar weakness with the U.S. flat on its face," said Jones. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020619dy6j00svu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
