\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar hits 17-month low vs euro on US stocks. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Kazunori Takada \par \uc2 687 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juni 2002\par 09:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 19 (Reuters) - Weakening dollar sentiment pushed down the greenback to a 17-month low against the euro on Wednesday as traders fretted over the feeble U.S. stock market and rising tensions in the Middle East. \par \par \uc2  The European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose as high as 95.43 cents in early Asian trade before settling down around 95.33, slightly firmer than 95.20 in late New York. Traders said the next key resistance was seen at 95.95, a high marked on January 5, 2001. \par \par \uc2  Sentiment remained weak for the dollar due to slipping Nasdaq and S&P 500 futures prices after disappointing reports from tech companies, and traders said this could push up the euro further. \par \par \uc2  "It (recent \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements) has a lot more to do with sentiment than economics," said Marshall Gittler, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bank of America in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, markets ignored strong U.S. data showing an 11.6 percent jump in housing construction in May, the biggest percentage rise in seven years and reversing two straight months of declines. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar is now completely separated from U.S. economic fundamentals," said Seiya Nakajima, an economist at Japanese trading house Itochu Corp. \par \par \uc2  The dollar suffered from news that Israel would retake parts of the West Bank after another suicide bombing. \par \par \uc2  Traders were also anxious about a media report that the White House has recently taken steps to let the CIA conduct \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  to oust Iraqi President Saddam Hussein. \par \par \uc2  "It seems nowadays that there is a flight out of dollar assets on the idea that rising tension in the Middle East will reflect most in the United States," said Bank of America's Gittler. \par \par \uc2  Sterling held firm near a 17-month high, supported around $1.4915 after hitting $1.4931 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  YEN IN ANOTHER WORLD \par \par \uc2  But all these worries about the dollar did little for the yen. \par \par \uc2  The greenback remained steady at 124.25 yen, little moved against 124.31 in late New York, supported only by fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "With the BOJ standing there and preventing the yen from further appreciating, traders are taking a shot at the euro since that has more upside potential," Gittler said. \par \par \uc2  The euro was maintaining a firm tone against the yen at 118.40 yen against 118.33 in late U.S. trade. \par \par \uc2  Some players said recent fund inflows to Japan are starting to show signs of abating and this could push the euro higher against the yen. \par \par \uc2  "Foreign investors' buying of Japanese stocks has become moderate these days," said Kazunari Kobayashi, treasury manager at State Street in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  "Japanese investors will have to invest abroad in the end because there are not many investment opportunities at home. \par \par \uc2  "So I think we are now at the stage to see whether the euro can rise above 120 yen and hold up there," Kobayashi added. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0547 GMT. All data taken from Reuters with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 GMT. \par \par \uc2   Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   2001 Cls \par \par \uc2   18 Jun. \par \par \uc2   ---------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/dlr       0.9529   0.9520   +0.09    +7.02   0.8904\par  Dlr/yen        124.23   124.31   -0.06   