\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar slips against buoyant euro ahead of Wall St. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Natsuko Waki \par \uc2 588 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 2002\par 12:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 18 (Reuters) - The dollar stepped back to come within sight of its 17-month trough against the euro on Tuesday as investors doubted whether Wall Street could sustain its tentative bounce in the previous session. \par \par \uc2  But the greenback managed to chalk up some gains against the yen as the market remained nervous about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  U.S. stocks jumped on Monday with the tech-driven Nasdaq rallying more than three percent. But U.S. stock futures were pointing to a lower opening on the day. \par \par \uc2  "No one has conviction that it was truly a sustainable rally," said Trevor Dinmore, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Deutsche Bank. \par \par \uc2  Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official Zembei Mizoguchi said earlier he would continue to monitor \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates closely. Japan, concerned about its exporters' competitiveness, has sold yen on at least four days in recent weeks. \par \par \uc2  "We're seeing a bout of yen weakness. The Japanese authorities are maintaining their stance against yen strength," said Rob Hayward, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN-Amro. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Japanese trust banks and pension funds had been big buyers of euros for yen, pushing the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 118.27 yen by 1015 GMT, within a yen of its five-month high set last week. \par \par \uc2  This dragged the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  up to a high of $0.9485, within half a cent of last week's 17-month peak. \par \par \uc2  The dollar rose to 124.75 from 124.28 in late New York on Monday. \par \par \uc2  SNB RAISES REPO \par \par \uc2  The Swiss franc was steady versus the euro and the dollar on Tuesday after the Swiss National Bank raised its repo rate by one basis point to one percent. \par \par \uc2  The repo rate had been at 0.99 percent since May 30 after the SNB started nudging rates gradually lower in late March to counter the impact of the strong Swiss franc. \par \par \uc2  SNB Vice Chairman Bruno Gehrig said the bank welcomed the euro's recent gains against the Swiss franc. He added the bank has no bias towards raising or cutting rates. \par \par \uc2  SNB Chairman Jean-Pierre Roth said last week the bank would rather see the euro at 1.47 francs than at lows around 1.44 it saw late last year. The SNB left its benchmark rate target unchanged at its quarterly policy review last week. \par \par \uc2  "Now euro/Swiss is back around 1.4750, they probably feel confident of pushing rates up," said Hayward. \par \par \uc2  But the Swiss franc paid little reaction and hugged narrow ranges near 1.4757, barely changed from late New York levels on Monday. Against the dollar it stood at 1.5580, compared with 1.5626 in late New York on Monday. \par \par \uc2  PERSISTENT CONCERNS \par \par \uc2  Later in the day, U.S. May consumer price data and May housing starts will be released. But the main focus is on U.S. trade data for April and current account figures for the first quarter, both due on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "We are still seeing flows into the U.S. but it is not sufficient enough to finance its current account deficit," Dinmore said. \par \par \uc2  Both of Thursday's sets of data are expected to show widening deficits. \par \par \uc2  Traders also looked towards the announcement of the Bank of Japan's corporate sentiment "tankan" survey on July 1. \par \par \uc2  Though the report is expected to show an improvement compared with the previous survey, some traders said it would not automatically trigger further yen-buying against the dollar. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020618dy6i00kzz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
