\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Kuroda-Japan to act in  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  markets if needed. \b0\par\par\uc2 546 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juni 2002\par 21:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 17 (Reuters) - Japan's top financial diplomat, Haruhiko Kuroda, said on Monday yen appreciation was inappropriate and Japan would continue to monitor markets and may act in markets if necessary. \par \par \uc2  Kuroda, Vice Minister of Finance for International Affairs, also said ratings given by credit agencies for Japanese government bonds were too low and should be adjusted upward. \par \par \uc2  The minister was in London after attending a weekend meeting of G7 finance ministers in Canada. \par \par \uc2  "Our exchange rate policy is quite simple - exchange rates should reflect fundamentals. We will continue to monitor market developments. If necessary we may act in the markets," Kuroda said in a question-and-answer session after making a speech at the Royal Institute of International Affairs. \par \par \uc2  His remarks added to a string of recent comments by Japanese officials who have loudly protested that a strengthening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could harm \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's tentative export-led recovery. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell yen for dollars on four days since late May. The yen has gained more than 5.0 percent against the greenback since January due mainly to concerns about U.S. asset markets and accounting practices in Corporate America. \par \par \uc2  Kuroda said of the recently strengthening euro: "Certainly the euro has been undervalued and now the euro has recovered. It's welcome. But the yen is not the case. Yen appreciation is not appropriate." \par \par \uc2  By 1842 GMT, the yen stood at 124.32 per dollar compared with levels beyond 124 at which \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent weeks. The yen hit a six-month high of 122.77 in late May. With traders hearing little new in his comments, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets were unmoved by Kuroda. \par \par \uc2  Against the euro, the yen stood at 117.33. \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has gained around 6.0 percent against the dollar since the beginning of this year. \par \par \uc2  RATINGS TOO LOW \par \par \uc2  Kuroda was also questioned about Japan's credit ratings, which suffered a string of downgrades recently by international ratings agencies. \par \par \uc2  Moody's Investor Service cut its Japan's local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  credit rating for long-term debt by two notches to A2 from Aa3, awarding it the lowest credit rating among leading economies. \par \par \uc2  Kuroda said the credit agencies did not take into account Japan's low debt servicing costs, large current-account balance of payments surplus and strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. \par \par \uc2  "We believe that the ratings provided by the rating agencies are too low and should be adjusted upwards," he said. \par \par \uc2  Kuroda has previously slammed the Moody's downgrade as unjustifiable, saying the international agency should rethink its decision. \par \par \uc2  Comments by Kuroda are closely monitored in financial markets. In the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's annual personnel reshuffle this summer, the 57-year-old official is widely expected to resign after three years in the job. \par \par \uc2  Zembei Mizoguchi, chief of the ministry's international bureau, is widely tipped to replace Kuroda probably at the end of this month or after a "Asia-Europe Meeting" (ASEM) in early July. \par \par \uc2  Asked about the rumours of his departure, Kuroda said: "I have been Vice Minister of Finance for three years. So far no vice minister has served more than three years in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But I do not know anything about my future." \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020617dy6h012wc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
