\par\par \b \uc2  IMM speculators trim net long vs the dollar - CFTC. \b0\par\par\uc2 683 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juni 2002\par 22:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      Kyle Peterson \par \par \uc2      CHICAGO, June 14 (Reuters) - Speculators in IMM euro futures \par \par \uc2  scaled back a net long position to its lowest level since \par \par \uc2  mid-April during the one-week period ended June 11, according to \par \par \uc2  data released Friday by the Commodity Futures Trading \par \par \uc2  Commission. \par \par \uc2      The slight reduction in the net long position, to 28,367 \par \par \uc2  from 31,616 contracts, eases some of the pressure on the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cave under the weight of a likely profit-taking \par \par \uc2  spree by speculators, analysts said. \par \par \uc2      "It looks like there was a little profit-taking in the \par \par \uc2  euro," said Andrew Delano, market analyst at IDEAglobal. "They \par \par \uc2  are still fairly long. It at least gives it somewhat of a \par \par \uc2  downward bias in weeks ahead." \par \par \uc2      The CFTC's weekly IMM Commitments of Traders data on \par \par \uc2  speculative positioning is used by many analysts as a reverse \par \par \uc2  indicator of future market direction. Extreme net long \par \par \uc2  speculative positions often presage a fall in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as \par \par \uc2  a turn in the market, which forces the speculators to fall in \par \par \uc2  line with the more influential players. \par \par \uc2      September euros continued their four-month-old rally \par \par \uc2  unabated this week, reaching a new contract high of $0.9489 by \par \par \uc2  Friday. The contract is primed for a mild correction, Delano \par \par \uc2  said. \par \par \uc2      Speculators in yen futures cut a net long position to its \par \par \uc2  smallest level since May 14. \par \par \uc2      "I think that part of this may have to do with the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the (Japanese) \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Delano \par \par \uc2  said. "This reporting period did include \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2      September yen spent the five sessions of the most recent \par \par \uc2  CFTC reporting period shedding some of the gains that carried it \par \par \uc2  to a 6-1/2-month high of $0.008185 on May 30. The contract has \par \par \uc2  been under pressure since reaching the recent peak amid \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen. \par \par \uc2  Japanese officials have complained that recent yen strength \par \par \uc2  is a hindrance to the export market and to the economy as a \par \par \uc2  whole. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, speculators in Canadian dollar futures stretched \par \par \uc2  a net long position to its highest since January 2000. \par \par \uc2  Nevertheless, September Canadian dollars shed gains during the \par \par \uc2  last reporting period. Losses continued through Friday when the \par \par \uc2  contract fell to a four-week low of $0.6482. The contract scored \par \par \uc2  a 10-month high of $0.6545 on June 4. \par \par \uc2  "It's still very imbalanced to the long side in Canada," \par \par \uc2  Delano said of the IMM positioning. "I think for the most part, \par \par \uc2  speculators are probably very willing to take profits." \par \par \uc2  Speculators in sterling futures extended a net long position \par \par \uc2  to its highest level since May 7. September sterling extended \par \par \uc2  gains to a contract high of $1.4720 on Friday. \par \par \uc2      "This would tend to argue for some correction in cable \par \par \uc2  (sterling) to the downside," Delano said. \par \par \uc2      Speculators in Mexican peso futures logged the lowest \par \par \uc2  position since the CFTC began collecting the data in 1995. \par \par \uc2  September peso futures spent the bulk of the reporting period \par \par \uc2  buoyed above 6-1/2-month low reached on June 7. \par \par \uc2      JAPANESE YEN (Contracts of 12,500,000 yen) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par              06/11/02 week         06/04/02 week\par    Long          17,774               17,715\par    Short         11,699                9,340\par    Net            6,075                8,375\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    EURO (Contracts of 125,000 euros)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par              06/11/02 week         06/04/02 week\par    Long          39,085               40,092\par    Short         10,718                8,476\par    Net           28,367               31,616\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    POUND STERLING (Contracts of 62,500 pounds sterling)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par              06/11/02 week         06/04/02 week\par    Long          16,657                9,819\par    Short          6,829                6,969\par    Net            9,828                2,850\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    SWISS FRANC (Contracts of 125,000 Swiss francs)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par              06/11/02 week         06/04/02 week\par    Long          15,115               14,226\par    Short          2,640                4,204\par    Net           12,475               10,022\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    CANADIAN DOLLAR (Contracts of 100,000 Canadian dollars)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par              06/11/02 week         06/04/02 week\par    Long          24,689               27,776\par    Short              0                4,498\par    Net           24,689               23,278\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    AUSTRALIAN DOLLAR (Contracts of 100,000 Aussie dollars)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par              06/11/02 week         06/04