\par\par \b \uc2  Japan's Kuroda heading to his last G7 as  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  chief. \b0\par\par\uc2 562 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juni 2002\par 12:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 14 (Reuters) - For Japan's top financial diplomat, Haruhiko Kuroda, this weekend's meeting of Group of Seven finance ministers will likely be his last as Vice Finance Minister For International Affairs. \par \par \uc2  In the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's annual personnel reshuffle this summer, 57-year-old Kuroda is widely expected to resign after three years in the job. \par \par \uc2  Zembei Mizoguchi, chief of the ministry's international bureau, is widely tipped to replace Kuroda probably at the end of this month or after a "Asia-Europe Meeting" (ASEM) in early July. \par \par \uc2  Comments from Kuroda and Mizoguchi frequently move financial markets. Recently, the two have been conveying the government's determination to prevent a resurgent yen from asphyxiating Jpaan's nascent export-led economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a foreign bank in Tokyo said he did not expect Mizoguchi to make big changes to \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. Still, some speculators may try to test Mizoguchi's position on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he added. \par \par \uc2  "There is a possibility that speculators will move the market to test his ability to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the trader said. \par \par \uc2  NO SURPRISE \par \par \uc2  The end of Kuroda's term and his replacement by Mizoguchi would be no surprise. \par \par \uc2  Traditionally, the longest term for vice finance ministers of international affairs is three years and Kuroda is seen as no exception. Also, the position has been replaced by the head of the international bureau in the past 20 years. \par \par \uc2  Mizoguchi, 56, joined the ministry in 1968. He has a wide range of experience, including jobs in the international bureau, budget bureau and the ministry's secretariat. He also worked in Japan's embassies in Germany and the United States. \par \par \uc2  As head of the Finance Ministry's international development policy division from 1989 to 1992, he was credited with helping prepare debt reduction plans for countries such as Egypt and Poland, both emerging economies and recipients of Japanese aid. \par \par \uc2  Mizoguchi is well known among journalists for his polite responses, even when talking to reporters half his age. He is typically cautious in making comments on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , avoiding comments that could be out of line with the ministry's stance. \par \par \uc2  "As far as we understand, he thinks stable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements are important so I don't think there will be a big impact on markets," said Koji Fukaya, chief analyst at the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  division of the Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi, referring to Mizoguchi's possible replacement of Kuroda. \par \par \uc2  But another market analyst said: "There is a saying that the position makes the person, so we have to see how (he) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market." \par \par \uc2  "When former vice finance minister for international affairs Eisuke Sakakibara replaced Kuroda, there were views that Kuroda would be more cautious about \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But in reality, Kuroda actively conducted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he added. \par \par \uc2  During Sakakibara's two-year term from July 15, 1997 to July 7, 1999, Japan stepped into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market a total of 18 days, conducting 8.65 trillion yen ($69.20 billion) in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  While Kuroda was in the job, Tokyo acted in the market on 24 days between July 8, 1999 to the end of March 2002, conducting 9.55 trillion yen in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Since March, Tokyo has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at least on four separate days, but the amount has not yet been publicised. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020614dy6e00kiz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
