\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar holds on to gains, but still vulnerable. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Chikafumi Hodo \par \uc2 814 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juni 2002\par 08:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 13 (Reuters) - The dollar on Thursday held on to recent gains against the yen and was steady against the euro, supported by a firm U.S. stock market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But the greenback remains vulnerable against the bullish euro and its topside is blocked against the yen by heavy sell orders from Japanese exporters, they said. \par \par \uc2  "Firmness in share prices lifted the dollar, but steady selling pressure from exporters was gradually weighing on the dollar," a senior interbank dealer at a Japanese bank said. \par \par \uc2  At 0600 GMT, the euro was little changed at $0.9440/43 against Wednesday's late U.S. level of $0.9434/39. \par \par \uc2  It rose to a 17-month high of $0.9507 on Wednesday but was pulled back after Wall Street stocks ended in positive territory. \par \par \uc2  The Dow Jones industrial closed 1.06 percent higher at 9,617.21 while the Nasdaq Composite Index gained 1.47 percent to 1,519.12. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro stood at 118.70/81 yen from 118.59/71. \par \par \uc2  Exporters showed strong interest in selling dollars around 125.70-125.80 yen, a level at which three-months forward contracts allow them to lock in dollar proceeds at around 125 yen, given the current forward discount of around 0.70 yen. \par \par \uc2  They also sold euros forward heavily on Wednesday after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  climbed to a five-month high of 119.27 yen. \par \par \uc2  "Many exporters are willing to sell euros using forward contracts around 119 yen," the senior dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted at 125.72/77 yen against Wednesday's late U.S. level of 125.65/70. \par \par \uc2  Japanese securities firms were detected buying the dollar and the Australian dollar against the yen on behalf of retail investors, who are showing interest in putting their summer bonuses into U.S. Treasuries and Aussie dollar bonds. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar/yen rate was little changed from Wednesday, but well-bid at 71.52/63 yen. \par \par \uc2  COMPLAINTS ON \b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  Although the dollar/yen reacted little, traders took note of a letter sent to U.S. Treasury Secretary Paul O'Neill by 24 U.S. lawmakers complaining about what they called Japan's meddling with \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates. \par \par \uc2  "Ahead of the U.S. interim election (in November), we're expecting to hear many complaints about \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . These comments should have a psychological impact in limiting heavy dollar-buying," a Japanese trust bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  House Small Business Committee Chairman Donald Manzullo, who headed the committee discussing the issue, called on O'Neill to put pressure on countries like Japan and China to stop manipulating their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar's value must be determined by market forces, not government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . I call on our government to step back and let the dollar correct itself," he said in a statement. \par \par \uc2  Japanese monetary authorities have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market at least four times since late May and are estimated to have bought over two trillion yen worth of dollars for yen. \par \par \uc2  The lawmakers asked O'Neill to convey their disapproval at a meeting of Group of Seven finance ministers to be held in Halifax, Canada, on June 14-15. \par \par \uc2  Japan's top financial diplomat, Haruhiko Kuroda, said \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates and monetary policy would not be on the agenda at Halifax but a Canadian finance official did not rule out the possibility, saying \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  issues often come up in G7 meetings. \par \par \uc2  Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the country's current account surplus in April rose by 21.7 percent from a year earlier to 1.085 trillion yen ($8.66 billion). \par \par \uc2  "The market was expecting a bigger figure so it would be a yen-selling factor. But because it was not the centre of focus, it had little effect on the market," said Toru Umemoto, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Morgan Stanely in Tokyo. ($1=125.24 yen). \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0609 GMT. All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 \par \par \uc2  GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                        Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   2001 Cls\par                                 12 Jun.\par                        -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr              0.9435   0.9430   +0.05    -0.64   0.9496\par  Dlr/yen               125.76   125.70   +0.05    +9.88   114.45\par  Euro/yen              118.67   118.59   +0.07    +9.16   108.71\par  Dlr/swiss             1.5639   1.5655   -0.10    -2.33   1.6012\par  Stg/dlr               1.4696   1.4706   -0.07    -2.03   1.5000\par  Can/dlr               1.5371   1.5349   +0.14    +3.06   1.4914\par  Aus/dlr               0.5687   0.5701   -0.25    +1.66   0.5594\par  Euro/swiss            1.4761   1.4776   -0.10    -3.02   1.5221\par  Euro/stg              0.6421   0.6415   +0.09    +1.52   0.6325.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020613dy6d00cti\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngbl