\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro marches to 17-mth high as Wall St dogs dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Natsuko Waki \par \uc2 570 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juni 2002\par 11:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 12 (Reuters) - The euro marched higher to a 17-month peak against the dollar and a five-month high versus the yen on Wednesday as persistent gloom on Wall Street encouraged investors to diversify out of U.S. and into euro zone assets. \par \par \uc2  The euro rose above the psychologically important level of $0.95 for the first time since January 2001 and hit five-month highs near 119.30 yen. \par \par \uc2  Lingering worries over corporate earnings and U.S. accounting standards sent the Dow Jones industrial average to its lowest close since November on Tuesday. U.S. stock futures were pointing to a lower open, keeping investors nervous. \par \par \uc2  "Investors are cutting back their exposure to U.S. assets and the euro is benefiting from it. The market is watching how equities markets open and react later," said Stacey Seltzer, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Brown Brothers Harriman. \par \par \uc2  Determination by Japanese authorities to curb export-damaging yen strength also gave investors reason to sell yen. \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell yen for dollars on four days since late May, concerned that a strengthening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could harm Japan's tentative export-led recovery. \par \par \uc2  The dollar stood at 125.50 yen in mid European trade, near Tuesday's three-week high of 125.80 yen, having tumbled to six-month lows below 123 yen set at the end of May. \par \par \uc2  US STOCKS DOMINATE \par \par \uc2  Attention was now focused on this week's U.S. economic indicators for more clues about the state of the world's biggest economy. \par \par \uc2  But important data, including retail sales on Thursday, is clustered at the end of this week, with Wednesday's Federal Reserve's Beige Book summary of economic conditions due at 1800 GMT only giving information of secondary importance. \par \par \uc2  That left investors keeping a close eye on the fate of Wall Street, which has been the dominant force in recent weeks in driving the dollar lower across the board. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar is still taking a beating from U.S. equity markets and the euro's short-term uptrend remains intact," said Paul Mackel, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Dresdner Kleinwort Wasserstein. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been successful in putting a floor under dollar/yen, so the euro is reaping most of the benefit." \par \par \uc2  JAPAN INFLOWS SLOW \par \par \uc2  The yen was unmoved by the Bank of Japan's widely-expected decision to maintain its super-loose monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  Most economists said Japan's recovery is still too fragile to talk of higher rates. \par \par \uc2  Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said net purchases of Japanese stocks by foreign investors rose to 931.7 billion yen ($7.44 billion) in May from April's net buying of 545.7 billion yen. \par \par \uc2  But the pace of the buying seems to have slowed significantly in June due to such negative factors as the yen's depreciation, declining Tokyo stock prices and tumbling shares on Wall Street. \par \par \uc2  In fact, foreign investors bought only 60.5 billion yen worth of Japanese stocks in the final week of May, a steep fall from 435.9 billion in the third week of the month. \par \par \uc2  Traders said this suggested upward pressure on the yen, generated by demand for stocks, may have run out of steam. \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors bought net 894.9 billion yen worth of bonds in May, versus net selling of 927.5 billion yen in April. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020612dy6c00kdh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
