\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar steady, but euro still on offensive. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Yoshiko Mori \par \uc2 791 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 2002\par 05:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 11 (Reuters) - The dollar was steady in late morning Tokyo trading on Tuesday, but the euro stayed on the offensive due to investor wariness towards U.S. asset markets and U.S.-Europe interest rate differentials favourable for the euro. "It's a game of finding who has fewer negatives," said Hideki Hayashi, global strategist at Shinko Securities. \par \par \uc2  No major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has decisively positive factors that lure global investors' money, but the euro has fewer negatives compared with the dollar and the yen, and thus is being chosen for their portfolios, he said. \par \par \uc2  Adding to ailing U.S. stocks, word from Washington that authorities had foiled a possible "dirty bomb" attack gave nervous investors more reason to shift out of the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The euro tested session highs versus the dollar on Monday in New York after the U.S. Justice Department said authorities had captured an American al-Qaeda operative who was planning to build and explode a radiological dispersion device, known as a dirty bomb. \par \par \uc2  But the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pared those gains as the dollar found footing against key \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after U.S. stocks held above earlier lows hit following the scare. \par \par \uc2  At 0225 GMT, the euro stood at $0.9445/50, up slightly from $0.9442 in late New York. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted at 124.66/71 yen, mostly unchanged from New York's 124.65 yen. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at 117.59/75 yen compared with 117.72 in New York. The euro earlier rose to 117.83 yen. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONIST\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS NON-\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONIST\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  Traders pointed to a clear difference in stance between policymakers in Japan and the euro zone towards appreciation of their own \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Senior Finance Ministry official Zembei Mizoguchi said on Tuesday there was no change in the ministry's stance that Japan will take action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if needed. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market several times since late May, buying dollars for yen. The amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is estimated to have reached well over 2.0 trillion yen ($16 billion), traders said. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, euro-zone policymakers have been showing a hands-off approach towards the euro's recent appreciation, making traders speculate that the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could soon test its 17-month high of $0.9595 hit in January 2001. \par \par \uc2  European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Wim Duisenberg said last Thursday that he was satisfied with the recent developments of the euro \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate. \par \par \uc2  Opinions are divided among economists over whether the market can take the ECB's comment at face value. \par \par \uc2  "When the euro was falling, euro-zone officials had said the fundamental strength of the euro-zone economy was not correctly reflected in the euro's value and that the euro had a lot more room to appreciate," said Shuichi Obata, economist at Nomura Research Institute. \par \par \uc2  "In light of this, I don't think euro-zone officials will start to complain about the strong euro anytime soon," he said. He forecast that the ECB would keep its hands-off approach at least until the euro rises to parity versus the dollar. \par \par \uc2  But others had different views. \par \par \uc2  "A further rapid rise in the euro would be unfavourable for European exporters as well as for fragile economic recovery in Europe," Shinko's Hayashi said. \par \par \uc2  "The ECB might feel comfortable about seeing the euro rise to around $0.9600, but corporate Europe could start to complain if it rose beyond that level, and then the ECB might change its policy tone towards the euro slightly," he added. \par \par \uc2  Data released by the Commodity Futures Trading Commission on Friday showed that while speculators scaled back net long euro positions in the week ended June 4, long positions remained near the record highs reached in early May. ($1=124.74 yen). \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0232 GMT. All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 \par \par \uc2  GMT. \par \par \uc2  Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   2001 Cls \par \par \uc2  10 Jun. \par \par \uc2  ----------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr              0.9442   0.9437   +0.05    -0.57   0.9496\par Dlr/yen               124.64   124.75   -0.09    +8.90   114.45\par Euro/yen              117.73   117.72   +0.01    +8.30   108.71\par Dlr/swiss             1.5583   1.5590   -0.04    -2.68   1.6012\par Stg/dlr               1.4606   1.4603   +0.02    -2.63   1.5000\par Can/dlr               1.5380   1.5394   -0.09    +3.12   1.4914\par Aus/dlr               0.5684   0.5698   -0.25    +1.61   0.5594\par Euro/swiss            1.4718   1.4720   -0.01    -3.30   1.5221\par Euro/stg              0.6462   0.6462   +0.00    +2.17   0.6325.\par \tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020611dy6b00ezb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
