\par\par \b \uc2  Want to bet on yen strength? Try Taiwan dlr options. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Anchalee Worrachate \par \uc2 638 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juni 2002\par 11:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, June 7 (Reuters) - Looking for a cheap way to ride on the coat-tails of a strengthening yen against the dollar? Taiwan dollar options may be your answer, analysts say. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan may not seem like the obvious place to make a bet on the world's two largest economies. \par \par \uc2  But analysts have some compelling reasons for viewing the tiny Taiwan dollar options market as the safest place in Asia to take advantage of a weak dollar/yen. \par \par \uc2  Despite its strong correlation to the yen - a result of trade ties and investor perception - the Taiwan dollar has been held back by the island's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently to ensure a stable exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  "Given its strong growth outlook, many in the market are still convinced the Taiwan dollar is undervalued and has more room for gains, although they might wait for some consolidation," said a dealer at a U.S. bank in Singapore. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists said many players were betting the U.S. dollar would soon head south again despite \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the yen's recovery in recent weeks. \par \par \uc2  The dollar has lost nearly seven percent against the yen since early April, due largely to a patchy U.S. recovery and signs of life in moribund Japan. \par \par \uc2  Instead of just buying a dollar/yen put option - a contract which gives buyers the right to sell the dollar at certain prices - these players should opt for a dollar/Taiwan dollar play, they said. \par \par \uc2  Ron Leven, regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Lehman Brothers, said a U.S. dollar/Taiwan dollar put option is the cheapest proxy for a long yen position against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "We feel that USD/TWD options are a relatively attractive way to position for further USD/JPY weakness," he said. \par \par \uc2  "If the dollar/yen goes a lot lower very quickly, the dollar/Taiwan dollar will go down as well though not as fast. But if the Bank of Japan comes in to support the dollar, you are not going to lose value quickly in the Taiwan dollar," he said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the Taiwan dollar's implied volatility, a key ingredient for pricing options, also remains low. \par \par \uc2  Volatility in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options measures the expected range in the value of an asset over the period of the contract, and is used to calculate options. Premium is affected by volatility, interest rates, strike price and expiration date. \par \par \uc2  Leven said he had recently recommended clients buy 3-month U.S. dollar/Taiwan dollar put options. He said the Taiwan dollar's implied volatility was currently around 3.7 percent versus 8.7 percent for the yen. \par \par \uc2  BEST OF BOTH WORLDS \par \par \uc2  So, what makes this trade a cheap and an attractive bet? The island's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might have a lot to do with it. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan adopted a floating exchange rate regime in April 1989. Although the value of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is generally determined by market forces, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is known to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly to keep the exchange rate stable. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  being a major trade partner and also a competitor, a strengthening yen means more room for the Taiwan dollar to rise without compromising competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  Lehman Brothers' Leven estimated the Taiwan dollar's correlation to the yen had risen above 50 percent this year from just around 20 percent in the past few years. \par \par \uc2  And even though Taiwan is experiencing an export-led economic rebound, like much of East Asia, its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not let its guard down and continues to rein in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation on a regular basis. \par \par \uc2  "Keeping the Taiwan dollar undervalued is seen as necessary to subsidise traditional industries and to discourage Taiwanese firms' investment in China," said Steve Xu, regional economist at SG Research in Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020607dy6700hrj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
