\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro hits 4-month high vs yen, dollar bearish. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Hideyuki Sano \par \uc2 708 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juni 2002\par 05:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 7 (Reuters) - The euro edged up to a four-month high against the yen on Friday, with operators switching into the European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from a bearish dollar and fears of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  holding the yen down. \par \par \uc2  The euro rose to a high of 117.98 yen and as of 0250 GMT stood at 117.85/96 yen . \par \par \uc2  The euro was also firmer against the dollar at 94.68/78 cents , just off its 17-month peak of 94.79 hit on Thursday, and up slightly from 94.63 cents in late U.S. trade. \par \par \uc2  The dollar edged up to 124.45/50 yen from around 124.23 in late U.S. trade but dealers said it was unlikely to top 125 yen, where many Japanese exporters were waiting to sell. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar failed its upside test on 125 yen three times," said Toshiyuki Aoyagi, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Nissho Iwai Financial Link. \par \par \uc2  Dealers were reluctant to bid up the yen since the BOJ has interevened four times in the past three weeks, buying the dollar for the yen each time the dollar has fallen below 124 yen. \par \par \uc2  "I think the authorities want to build a floor for the dollar around the 123 yen level," said said Kota Kimura, assistant manager at Shinkin \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Wariness about BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is so strong that the market hardly reacted to \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's January-March gross domestic product (GDP) data, which came in slightly above expectations. \par \par \uc2  Japan's real GDP rose 1.4 percent from the previous quarter versus median forecast of 1.3 percent. \par \par \uc2  That came after three consecutive quarters of contraction and confirmed Japan's economy is finally starting to pick up. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese authorities kept up their verbal pressure on the yen, saying they were ready to act in the market if needed. \par \par \uc2  Vice Finance Minister Haruhiko Kuroda said his ministry would take "bold action" in the markets as necessary, the addition of the world "bold" apparently underlining the authorities' seriousness, according to some traders. \par \par \uc2  INTEL SHOCK \par \par \uc2  The dollar has so far failed to capitalise on the BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , weighed down by the poor performance of U.S. equity markets in recent months. \par \par \uc2  The latest blow for the dollar came from a disappointing forecast from leading chipmaker Intel , which late on Thursday lowered its revenue forecast for the current quarter. \par \par \uc2  Intel's announcement, apart from pushing down its own share price after the bell, hit Nasdaq futures more than 30 points and looks set to hurt Wall Street, which hit a fresh eight-month low even before Intel's announcement. \par \par \uc2  The fact that strong U.S. economic indicators have been largely ignored by the market or have perhaps been outweighed by worries about accounting practices in Corporate America have made dealers think the dollar's problems are deep-rooted. \par \par \uc2  "U.S. economic indicators for May have been strong. But U.S. equities are in a different world," said Kota Kimura at Shinkin \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The market is for now focusing on the release of May U.S. employment data at 1230 GMT on Friday, which are expected to show a gain of 58,000 in non-farm jobs as well as a rise in the unemployment rate to 6.1 percent. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0304 GMT. All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 \par \par \uc2  GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                        Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   2001 Cls\par                                 06 Jun.\par                        -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr              0.9471   0.9470   +0.01    +6.37   0.8904\par  Dlr/yen               124.45   124.06   +0.31    -5.45   131.63\par  Euro/yen              117.85   117.56   +0.25    +0.52   117.24\par  Dlr/swiss             1.5556   1.5556   +0.00    -6.26   1.6594\par  Stg/dlr               1.4601   1.4605   -0.03    +0.41   1.4541\par  Can/dlr               1.5307   1.5325   -0.12    -3.83   1.5917\par  Aus/dlr               0.5747   0.5756   -0.16   +12.55   0.5106\par  Euro/swiss            1.4740   1.4743   -0.02    -0.27   1.4780\par  Euro/stg              0.6487   0.6486   +0.02    +5.94   0.6123.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020607dy67006mx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
