\par\par \b \uc2  GLOBAL YIELD: BOJ Ripples Spread In Tsys, Agency Debt \b0\par\par\uc2  By John Parry \par \uc2 797 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juni 2002\par 20:36\par \uc2  Dow Jones Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK -(Dow Jones)- The ripples of Japan's monetary policy are spreading. \par \par \uc2  Repercussions from the recent bout of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  - acting via the Bank of Japan - are accumulating in the U.S. Treasury and agency debt securities markets, as Japan uses its newly-acquired dollars to buy U.S. bonds. In the process, Japan is giving an additional helping hand in financing the U.S. current account deficit at a time when more and more foreign investors are shifting their funds elsewhere, or considering doing so. \par \par \uc2  The Federal Reserve's custody holdings on behalf of foreign banks showed a much larger-than-usual net increase of $17.3 billion for the week ending Wednesday - which fixed income and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analysts attribute largely to the MOF. Of the hefty increase, approximately $7 billion was invested in agency debt and the remainder in the Treasury market. The previous week, these holdings, a component of the Federal Reserve's weekly money supply data released each Thursday, had shown the institution's holdings of securities for foreign central banks climbed $8.7 billion, a figure that was already well above typical levels. \par \par \uc2  Although the Fed doesn't given a breakdown of who's doing the buying, the combined increase fits roughly with approximate estimates of the BOJ's four bouts of dollar purchases during the last two weeks, part of the finance ministry's bid to weaken the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and ward off any obstacles to a fragile cyclical rebound in the world's second-largest economy. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders estimate that Japan's combined purchases have amounted to approximately $20 billion, which analysts and other finance officials believe the BOJ - seeking some return on its newly-acquired dollars - has reinvested in U.S. bonds. "I would have to believe that (the increase in the Fed's custody holdings) is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related, it's extremely likely," said Gerald Lucas, senior government strategist with Merrill Lynch in New York. The Fed data for the past two weeks "most definitely" reflects the aftermath of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Lucas added. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Biggest Weekly Jump In 15 Months\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Last week's net jump was the biggest since March 2001, when there was\par an $18.5 billion increase in one week, Lucas noted. Normal weekly moves\par tend to range between just $3 billion to $4 billion, in either the plus\par or minus column.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Federal Reserve acts as a custodian in accounts it maintains on\par behalf of foreign official institutions, including central banks. The\par Fed doesn't specify which institutions have made transactions, or even\par their nationalities.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In this sense, it's certainly probable that some part of the hefty net\par increase may be unrelated to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and\par attributable to other foreign central banks making transactions. But the\par magnitude of the increase has led market watchers to safely assume that\par a large chunk of it can be traced to the BOJ.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "In large measure it's the BOJ," behind the increase, said Lou\par Crandall, chief economist at Wrightson Associates Inc, a New-York based\par economic research company.  Aside from the total number, "what caught\par peoples' eyes was the jump in agency holdings: $7 billion is a pretty\par big purchase for that market," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Scott Graham, co-head of the agency department at Greenwich Capital\par Markets, noted that this "helps explain the recent improvement" in the\par performance of shorter-dated agency debt securities\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the Bank of Japan generally tend to invest\par mostly in shorter-dated bills and notes, up to about two-years maturity,\par but sometimes buy somewhat longer-dated paper out to five years.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par While Graham expects this flow to have "a positive impact" on agency\par securities' prices, Crandall notes that the shorter end of the Treasury\par market has already capitalized to some degree on the side-effects of the\par BOJ's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market actions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Two-year Treasury note yields, which move inversely to their prices,\par "have fallen over the past couple of weeks, despite the fact that (U.S.)\par economic data on balance have been relatively firm," Crandall said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Signs of a more robust economy would normally send Treasury yields\par higher on expectations of interest rate hikes, although it is true that\par the Treasury bond market has also done better recently because it has\par captured a flight-to-quality bid from sliding U.S. equities.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Friday afternoon in New York, the two-year's yield had slid to 3.14%,\par down from 3.23% two weeks ago.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -By John Parry; Dow Jones Newswires\par    john.parry@dowjones.com; 201-938-2096\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Michael S. Derby and Tyler Lifton contributed to this report).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4083 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020020607dy670086h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
