\par\par \b \uc2  Euro/Dlr/Highs -2: Still Holding Around Key Levels \b0\par\par\uc2 581 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juni 2002\par 18:26\par \uc2  Dow Jones Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Traders said the euro has broken above some key levels, capitalizing on the dollar's despondent tone. \par \par \uc2  "If we can hold above $0.9450, we could see $0.9600 and some people are talking about parity," said John Cholakis, trader at Natexis Banques Populaire in New York. \par \par \uc2  At 12:10 p.m. EDT, the euro had pared some of its earlier gains but was nevertheless in that range, at about $0.9450. \par \par \uc2  Equity weakness was the key catalyst for the dollar's relapse midday Thursday, said John McCarthy, director of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at ING Barings Capital Markets in New York. \par \par \uc2  "What we are seeing is continued concern about the value of equities here, and in general," McCarthy said. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar is still under pressure," he said. "Just when you think that the dollar has bottomed out for the time  being, then that's not the case", he said. \par \par \uc2  Despite some initial disappointment that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left interest rates unchanged, as expected, at its policy meeting earlier Thursday, the euro was to some extent bolstered by stronger economic data from Europe's biggest economy released earlier in the global day. \par \par \uc2  German manufacturing orders rose in April for the first time this year, and much more strongly than analysts  had estimated, offering clearer evidence of a long-awaited economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  Yet even long term euro bulls are skeptical of the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength. \par \par \uc2  "I'm not sure if it's a fundamental euro rally, there are not too many reasons to buy the euro," said Jan Poser, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at Sarasin Bank in Zurich. \par \par \uc2  Adding to the suspicion that Thursday's euro gains may not be a reliable guide to broad market sentiment, traders point out that the dollar's weakness is quite selective, with some \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  gaining along with the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,  while others have failed to climb to new cyclical highs. \par \par \uc2  On the negative side for the dollar, the U.S. unit  has fallen to new multi-month lows versus the commodity \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Australia, New Zealand and South Africa, with investors' ongoing risk aversion also boosting the safe-haven driven Swiss franc. \par \par \uc2  But dollar-bulls are able to point to some positive straws in the wind. \par \par \uc2  Against its Canadian counterpart, the dollar has recovered more than half-a-cent from its 23-month low seen earlier this week, with one analyst commenting that the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise, "has got ahead of itself". \par \par \uc2  Although it has dropped three-quarters of a yen in New York from its intraday high, the dollar is still holding well above last week's 6-month low against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with dealers nervous of adding to their yen holdings for fear of being caught on the wrong side of another round of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "I think people are very reluctant to sell dollars against yen," said John Cholakis, trader at Natexis Banques Populaires in New York. \par \par \uc2  Despite solid economic backing, the pound is essentially  flat against the dollar as \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets continue to act  on the view that signs of pro-euro sentiment in the U.K. will lead to a long term trend of selling the pound against the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , also undermining its rate versus the greenback. \par \par \uc2  -By John Hardy, Dow Jones Newswires; 201-938-2122; john.hardy@dowjones.com and John Parry, Dow Jones Newswires, 201-938-2096; john.parry@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020020606dy66007vd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
