\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar soft but holds Y124 on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Kazunori Takada \par \uc2 479 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 2002\par 08:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 5 (Reuters) - The dollar held just above Japan's apparent defence line of 124 yen on Wednesday after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again during New York hours, but traders expect more pressure ahead as investors continue to shun U.S. assets. \par \par \uc2  "The market's focus is now clearly on the trend in the U.S. asset market, and in that environment economic indicators from Japan and elsewhere have to take a back seat," said Minori Takeuchi, vice president at Chase Manhattan Bank. The dollar took no notice of Japanese Finance Ministry data showing that companies scaled back capital investment in January-March for a second straight quarter as they focused on trimming inventories. \par \par \uc2  As of 0533 GMT, the dollar stood at 124.00 yen slightly off the late U.S. level of 124.12. \par \par \uc2  Traders are wary of selling the dollar too aggressively fearing more action by Japanese authorities to stem the yen's rise. \par \par \uc2  The euro inched up to 94.08 cents from 93.92 cents in late New York. It also ticked up against the yen to 116.73 from 115.58. \par \par \uc2  BEARISH DOLLAR CONTINUES \par \par \uc2  During early U.S. trading hours, Japanese monetary authorities confirmed they had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, for the fourth day in two weeks. That sent the dollar up around one yen to 124.34 yen in New York. \par \par \uc2  "Basically, what is giving the dollar support right now is the BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Koichi Abe, manager at Aozora Bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading section. \par \par \uc2  Japan's top financial diplomat, Haruhiko Kuroda, reiterated warnings on Wednesday that the Finance Ministry was ready to take action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as needed and that they were continuing to keep a close watch on market movements. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have done little to change the dollar's bearish sentiment. \par \par \uc2  "I think the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are just absorbing the foreigners' capital inflows (to \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 )," Abe said. \par \par \uc2  Finance Ministry data showed last week that foreign investors bought a net 435.9 billion yen ($3.51 billion) of Japanese stocks in the week of May 20-24, up from the previous week's 359.2 billion yen. \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors have been net buyers of Japanese stocks since March, scooping up more than 1.8 trillion yen worth, after offloading a net 269.2 billion yen between December and February. European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data last week showed portfolio and direct investment in the euro zone saw a combined inflow of 2.2 billion euros in March, compared with a net outflow of 19.8 billion euros in February. \par \par \uc2  The European single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose to a fresh 16-month high of $0.9453 in New York on Tuesday, staging a recovery of over 10 percent from this year's low around $0.8563 in early February. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020606dy6500dl8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
