\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar steady,  \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention \highlight\uc2  warnings heeded. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Christina Fincher \par \uc2 462 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 2002\par 10:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 5 (Reuters) - The dollar was steady across the board on Wednesday with dealers nervous of pushing the greenback to new lows for fear of triggering another bout of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Japanese authorities waded into the market for the fourth day in two weeks on Tuesday, selling yen for dollars in a bid to curb the yen's recent export-damaging rise. \par \par \uc2  "Fear of more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is helping stabilise the dollar for now, but is only likely to slow the pace of the dollar's fall," said Francesca Fornasari, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Lehman Brothers. \par \par \uc2  The dollar tumbled to a 16-month low against the euro and a 2-1/2 year low against the Swiss franc on Tuesday as another poor performance on Wall Street raised concern of a decline in fund flows into dollar assets. \par \par \uc2  "Unless U.S. assets start to perform better, people will continue to look for investment opportunities elsewhere," Fornasari added. \par \par \uc2  The dollar stood at 124.20 yen , in early European trade, little changed on the day but up more than a yen from last week's six-month lows. The euro was changing hands just below $0.94 , more than half a cent away from Tuesday's highs. \par \par \uc2  Japan's top financial diplomat, Haruhiko Kuroda, kept traders on their toes, reiterating that the Finance Ministry was continuing to keep a close watch on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves. \par \par \uc2  CAPITAL FLOWS DOMINATE \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Ministry data showing companies scaled back capital investment in January-March for a second straight quarter had little impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  Most analysts still expect gross domestic product for that period, due on Friday, to show a strong rebound thanks to a recovery in exports and firm personal spending. \par \par \uc2  Japanese authorities confirmed on Tuesday they had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell the yen, helping send the dollar up around one yen to 124.34 in New York. \par \par \uc2  "Basically, what is giving the dollar support right now is the BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Koichi Abe, manager at Aozora Bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading section. \par \par \uc2  But he added the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were just absorbing capital inflows into \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and doing little to change the dollar's bearish sentiment. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Ministry data showed last week that foreign investors bought a net 435.9 billion yen ($3.51 billion) of Japanese stocks in the week of May 20-24, up from the previous week's 359.2 billion yen. \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors have been net buyers of Japanese stocks since March. \par \par \uc2  European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data last week showed portfolio and direct investment in the euro zone saw a combined inflow of 2.2 billion euros in March, compared with a net outflow of 19.8 billion euros in February. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020605dy6500flw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
