ef to investors worried about its effect on exporters' overseas profits when repatriated into the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  Sony Corp, the world's biggest consumer electronics maker which depends on the United States for one third of its sales, gained 1.45 percent to 6,980 yen. \par \par \uc2  In mid-morning Asian trade, the dollar was moving at around 124.09 yen, slightly weaker after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the fourth time in two weeks in Tuesday U.S. trading hours, selling yen for dollars to keep the yen in check. \par \par \uc2  Chipmakers were also back in favour after the Philadelphia semiconductor index rebounded 3.44 percent on Tuesday as investors took advantage of recent declines to snap up bargains. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo Electron, Japan's biggest manufacturer of chip equipment, was up 1.81 percent at 8,450 yen, while Toshiba Corp, Japan's largest chipmaker, put on 1.53 percent to 530 yen. \par \par \uc2  Losers included casual-wear leader Fast Retailing Co Ltd, down 7.55 percent at 2,940 after it said after the market close on Tuesday its same-store sales fell 44.2 percent in May from a year earlier.. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020605dy65004yi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
