\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Threat Keeps Dlr/Yen Bears At Bay \b0\par\par\uc2  By Audrey McAvoy \par \uc2 730 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juni 2002\par 07:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The dollar remained virtually unchanged against the yen in Asian trade Tuesday, as a holiday in the U.K. and the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities kept trade to a minimum. \par \par \uc2  But players said the dollar will likely resume sliding against the yen later in the global day, given the uncertain outlook for the U.S. stock markets and economy. \par \par \uc2  "It is hard to push the dollar/yen down in Tokyo hours as the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is always there," a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at a major Japanese bank said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is likely to follow a similar pattern to Monday, he said, when it stayed firm in Asian trade only to slide to an intraday low in New York. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar's slide is part of a shift in capital flows as foreign investors raise their investments in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to an appropriate level. I don't think \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can change the direction of these flows," the trader said. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is just adjusting the speed of the yen's rise," he added. \par \par \uc2  Players warned any break below the Y123.50 level may prompt the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ask the Bank of Japan to step into the market and stem the yen's rise. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa told a regular press conference Japan remains on guard against "unnatural" \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves, indicating the MOF is ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if needed. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  "moves have been a bit volatile. Our ultimate goal is stability," Shiokawa said. \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa added he is constantly watching the market's reaction to the ministry's efforts to normalize \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT (12:15 a.m. EST), the dollar was quoted at Y123.50, below Y123.56 late Monday in New York. The dollar was at Y124.33 late Monday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $0.9430, higher than $0.9411 late Monday in New York. The euro was at $0.9315 in Tokyo Monday. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y116.46, up from Y116.28 in New York late Monday. The euro was at Y115.85 in Tokyo late Monday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.4628, little changed from $1.4626 in New York but higher than $1.4561 in Tokyo Monday. \par \par \uc2  The euro rose to a 16-month high against the dollar as speculators selling the U.S. unit targeted the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after they found themselves unable to buy the yen, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a high of $0.9430 in intraday trade, its highest level since Feb. 5, 2001, when it rose as far as $0.9442. \par \par \uc2  "There was some profit-taking, but the euro is rising gradually as speculators buy the euro instead of the yen," said Kaneo Ogino, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at HSBC. \par \par \uc2  Lackluster U.S. stocks in the face of strong economic data also fueled the euro rise, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "U.S. fundamentals are steady but investors are fed up hearing about various companies' problems and fishy accounting," Ogino said. \par \par \uc2  The Dow Jones Industrial Average closed near its intraday low Monday, dropping 2.2%, or 215.46 points, to 9709.79 as shares declined on more concerns about profits, accounting and world unrest. \par \par \uc2  The Standard & Poor's 500 Index, which contains a variety of big-cap stocks, plunged 2.5% to 1040.68, marking a new low for the year. \par \par \uc2  Euro/dollar offers to protect an option with a knock-out trigger at $0.9450 should cap the upside for the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the meantime, however, Ogino said, though a break above $0.9450 should clear the way for a rise to $0.9600. \par \par \uc2  The euro will also be weighed down by offers to sell for yen at Y116.50 from Japanese exporters and other players, a trader at a Japanese bank said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   -By Audrey McAvoy, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929;\par audrey.mcavoy@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The chart of late Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates that accompanied Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has\par been replaced with an enhanced \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fixture, which is\par updated hourly.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Subscribers can find this table:\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX\par -0\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020604dy640009v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
