\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar up sharply vs. yen on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 241 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juni 2002\par 15:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  1328 GMT - Greenback extends gains vs. yen as \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen buying dollars. The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed it was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market but would not say in what \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Traders said they did not see action taking place in New York, leading to speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  used the overnight desks in Tokyo to carry out the orders. \par \par \uc2  - Aside from dollar strength against the yen, the greenback was broadly lower, falling to a fresh 16-month low against the euro, hit by heavy sales on Wall Street on Monday amid worries over the soundness of earnings statements, the prospect of war between nuclear rivals India and Pakistan, a steady rumble of terror alerts in the United States and slack corporate profits. \par \par \uc2  - Dollar/yen was at 124.05 yen, just off the session highs near 124.40 yen, a gain of 0.40 percent compared with Monday's New York close. \par \par \uc2  - The euro was trading at 94.26 cents, down from session highs of 94.53 cents, but up 0.15 percent on the day. The next psychological level for the euro would be 95.04 cents, which would put the greenback at its lowest level since the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since Jan. 15, 2001. \par \par \uc2  - The Dollar fell against the Swiss franc to a new 2-1/2 year low of 1.5535 francs, a drop of 0.40 percent. \par \par \uc2  -. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020604dy6400qpl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
